    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      35.18996810913086,
      832.7313232421875,
      81.38996887207031
    ],
    "text": "SHORT BIOGRAPHY : WHO IS RENE DESCARTES ?",
    "size": 33.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "2:1",
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      98.51997375488281,
      218.51226806640625,
      137.71998596191406
    ],
    "text": "Key dates: ",
    "size": 28.00000762939453,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 8355711
  },
  {
    "id": "2:2",
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      153.02403259277344,
      409.290771484375,
      477.1620178222656
    ],
    "text": "•\n1596 : date of birth in La Haye, France\n•\n1606 : starts his education at the jesuit \ncollege of La Fleche\n•\n1610 : Galileo discovers the moon of Jupiter \nat La Fleche\n•\n1618 : finishes his studies and moves to the \nNetherlands\n•\n1629 : publishes his Treaty on the Light\n•\n1637 : publishes his Discourse on the \nMethod\n•\n1641 : publishes his Meditations on First \nPhilosophy\n•\n1644 : publishes his Principles of philosophy\n•\n1650 : Dies in Sweden after having joined \nthe court of Queen Christina ",
    "size": 18.0,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "2:3",
    "page": 1,
    "bbox": [
      527.3253784179688,
      98.51997375488281,
      650.553466796875,
      137.71998596191406
    ],
    "text": "Portrait :",
    "size": 28.00000762939453,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 8355711
  },
  {
    "id": "3:0",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      69.57524108886719,
      33.96001052856445,
      855.7359619140625,
      84.3600082397461
    ],
    "text": "REBUILDING KNOWLEDGE: THE TABULA RASA",
    "size": 36.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:1",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      102.72002410888672,
      886.0014038085938,
      125.1200180053711
    ],
    "text": "« Suppose [a person] had a basket full of apples and, being worried that some of the apples were",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:2",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      130.79998779296875,
      885.8973999023438,
      153.19998168945312
    ],
    "text": "rotten, wanted to take out the rotten ones to prevent the rot spreading. How would he proceed? Would",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:3",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      159.84002685546875,
      885.9904174804688,
      182.24002075195312
    ],
    "text": "he not begin by tipping the whole lot out of the basket? And would not the next step be to cast his eye",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:4",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      188.8800048828125,
      885.88818359375,
      211.27999877929688
    ],
    "text": "over each apple in turn, and pick up and put back in the basket only those he saw to be sound, leaving",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:5",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      217.67999267578125,
      885.940185546875,
      240.07998657226562
    ],
    "text": "the others? In just the same way, those who have never philosophized correctly have various opinions in",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:6",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      246.72003173828125,
      885.9409790039062,
      269.1200256347656
    ],
    "text": "their minds which they have begun to store up since childhood, and which they therefore have reason",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:7",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      274.79998779296875,
      886.0016479492188,
      297.1999816894531
    ],
    "text": "to believe may in m any cases be false. They then attempt to separate the false beliefs from the others,",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:8",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      303.84002685546875,
      885.9515991210938,
      326.2400207519531
    ],
    "text": "so as to prevent their contaminating the rest and making the whole lot uncertain. Now the best way",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:9",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      332.8800048828125,
      885.8923950195312,
      355.2799987792969
    ],
    "text": "they can accomplish this is to reject all their beliefs together in one go, as if they were all uncertain and",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:10",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      361.67999267578125,
      885.9915771484375,
      384.0799865722656
    ],
    "text": "false. They can then go over each belief in turn and re-adopt only those which they recognize to be true",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:11",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      400.79998779296875,
      444.2010192871094,
      423.1999816894531
    ],
    "text": "and indubitable. (Replies 7, AT 7:481, CSM 2:324) »",
    "size": 15.99999713897705,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "3:12",
    "page": 2,
    "bbox": [
      227.1875,
      471.1199951171875,
      732.7489624023438,
      515.9199829101562
    ],
    "text": "THE BASKET OF APPLE ANALOGY",
    "size": 31.999990463256836,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "4:0",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      69.57524108886719,
      33.96001052856445,
      491.9740905761719,
      84.3600082397461
    ],
    "text": "DOUBTING OUR SENSES ",
    "size": 36.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:1",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      121.32000732421875,
      886.010009765625,
      149.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "« A soldier returns from battle; during the heat of combat he could have been",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:2",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      157.32000732421875,
      886.0050048828125,
      185.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "wounded without being aware of it. But now that he begins to cool off, he feels pain",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:3",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      193.32000732421875,
      885.8909912109375,
      221.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "and believes he has been wounded. A surgeon is called, the soldier's armor is",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:4",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      229.32000732421875,
      885.9650268554688,
      257.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "removed, and he is examined. In the end, one finds that what he felt was nothing",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:5",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      265.32000732421875,
      886.0,
      293.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "but a buckler or a strap, which was caught under his armor and was pressing on",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:6",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      301.32000732421875,
      885.9700317382812,
      329.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "him and making him uncomfortable. If, in causing him to feel this strap, his sense",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:7",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      337.32000732421875,
      885.9600219726562,
      365.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "of touch had impressed its image on his thought, there would have been no need",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:8",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      56.32503890991211,
      373.32000732421875,
      741.1699829101562,
      401.32000732421875
    ],
    "text": "of a surgeon to show him what he was feeling. (Treaty on the Light) »",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "4:9",
    "page": 3,
    "bbox": [
      211.3125,
      471.1199951171875,
      748.6500244140625,
      515.9199829101562
    ],
    "text": "THE WOUNDED SOLDIER ANALOGY",
    "size": 31.999990463256836,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "5:0",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      73.19999694824219,
      507.21600341796875,
      886.6589965820312,
      521.8680419921875
    ],
    "text": "25/11/2022\n5",
    "size": 12.0,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 9013641
  },
  {
    "id": "5:1",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      69.57524108886719,
      33.96001052856445,
      802.635986328125,
      84.3600082397461
    ],
    "text": "LAPLACE AND THE HYPERBOLICAL DOUBT ",
    "size": 36.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:2",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      113.6400146484375,
      875.4752197265625,
      141.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "“We may regard the present state of the universe as the effect of its past and the",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:3",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      149.6400146484375,
      875.3851928710938,
      177.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "cause of its future. An intellect which at a certain moment would know all forces",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:4",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      185.6400146484375,
      875.3911743164062,
      213.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "that set nature in motion, and all positions of all items of which nature is",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:5",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      221.6400146484375,
      875.5001831054688,
      249.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "composed, if this intellect were also vast enough to submit these data to",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:6",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      257.6400146484375,
      875.480224609375,
      285.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "analysis, it would embrace in a single formula the movements of the greatest",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:7",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      293.6400146484375,
      875.4652099609375,
      321.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "bodies of the universe and those of the tiniest atom; for such an intellect nothing",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:8",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      329.6400146484375,
      875.397216796875,
      357.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "would be uncertain and the future just like the past would be present before its",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:9",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      61.95022964477539,
      365.6400146484375,
      526.4451904296875,
      393.6400146484375
    ],
    "text": "eyes. (A philosophical Essay on probabilities) “",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Italic",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "5:10",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": [
      289.5625,
      471.1199951171875,
      670.50634765625,
      515.9199829101562
    ],
    "text": "THE DEMON OF LAPLACE",
    "size": 31.999990463256836,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "6:0",
    "page": 5,
    "bbox": [
      489.17498779296875,
      243.20001220703125,
      894.7390747070312,
      292.0400390625
    ],
    "text": "I THINK THEREFORE I AM",
    "size": 40.00000762939453,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "6:1",
    "page": 5,
    "bbox": [
      765.4099731445312,
      429.5199890136719,
      905.6199951171875,
      453.94000244140625
    ],
    "text": "RENÉ DESCARTES",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "6:2",
    "page": 5,
    "bbox": [
      666.7650146484375,
      465.5200500488281,
      905.8049926757812,
      489.9400634765625
    ],
    "text": "DISCOURSE ON THE METHOD",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 8355711
  },
  {
    "id": "6:5",
    "page": 5,
    "bbox": [
      69.57524108886719,
      33.96001052856445,
      850.7176513671875,
      84.3600082397461
    ],
    "text": "THE CARTESIAN COGITO : FIRST EXPRESSION",
    "size": 36.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "7:0",
    "page": 6,
    "bbox": [
      490.79998779296875,
      156.79998779296875,
      902.280029296875,
      334.760009765625
    ],
    "text": "I AM, I EXIST IS \nNECESSARILY TRUE \nEVERYTIME I SAY THIS \nSENTENCE OR CONCEIVE ",
    "size": 40.00000762939453,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "7:1",
    "page": 6,
    "bbox": [
      566.780029296875,
      328.87994384765625,
      817.152099609375,
      377.719970703125
    ],
    "text": "IT IN MY MIND.",
    "size": 40.00000762939453,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "7:2",
    "page": 6,
    "bbox": [
      765.4099731445312,
      429.5199890136719,
      905.6199951171875,
      453.94000244140625
    ],
    "text": "RENÉ DESCARTES",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "7:3",
    "page": 6,
    "bbox": [
      605.6699829101562,
      465.5200500488281,
      905.669921875,
      489.9400634765625
    ],
    "text": "MEDITATIONS ON FIRST PHILOSOPHY",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 8355711
  },
  {
    "id": "7:6",
    "page": 6,
    "bbox": [
      68.95024108886719,
      35.18996810913086,
      834.685546875,
      81.38996887207031
    ],
    "text": "THE CARTESIAN COGITO : SECOND EXPRESSION",
    "size": 33.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "8:0",
    "page": 7,
    "bbox": [
      880.5750122070312,
      507.21600341796875,
      886.6589965820312,
      521.8680419921875
    ],
    "text": "8",
    "size": 12.0,
    "font": "Calibri",
    "color": 9013641
  },
  {
    "id": "8:1",
    "page": 7,
    "bbox": [
      69.57524108886719,
      33.96001052856445,
      723.9365844726562,
      84.3600082397461
    ],
    "text": "THE CARTESIAN METHOD : SUMMARY",
    "size": 36.0,
    "font": "Poppins-Bold",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "8:2",
    "page": 7,
    "bbox": [
      201.70399475097656,
      117.47998046875,
      738.248046875,
      145.47998046875
    ],
    "text": "THE TABULA RASA  : Beginning of the methodical doubt",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "8:3",
    "page": 7,
    "bbox": [
      184.8914031982422,
      192.8399658203125,
      760.3754272460938,
      220.8399658203125
    ],
    "text": "THE HYPERBOLICAL DOUBT : Using the demon of Laplace to ",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "8:4",
    "page": 7,
    "bbox": [
      376.5765075683594,
      216.8399658203125,
      563.2164916992188,
      244.8399658203125
    ],
    "text": "push doubt further",
    "size": 19.999998092651367,
    "font": "Poppins-Regular",
    "color": 16777215
  },
  {
    "id": "8:5",
    "page": 7,
    "bbox": [
      292.40789794921875,
      291.9599609375,
      655.2998657226562,
      319.9599609375
    ],
